  "mismatches_note": "Briefing `sourceTier` values contradicting the tier the same-date assessment cites for the same URL. **43 entries, across only 3 briefing dates (2026-07-24, 2026-07-25, 2026-07-27) and 29 distinct URLs** — concentrated, not systemic. 27 OVERSTATE the evidence (the briefing claims a stronger tier than the assessment it cites) and 16 understate it. The worst overstate a blog as tier 5, the top tier: mineralanswers.com and veroscribe.com both carry T5 in a briefing against T2 and T1 in their assessments. The worst understatements are primary sources dropped to T1 — justice.gov (assessment T5), oig.hhs.gov (T5) and the UN's ukraine.ohchr.org (T4). CORRECTION TO THE RECORD: this list shipped EMPTY on 2026-09-30 (Iteration 71) claiming \"0 mismatches\" over 72 compared pairs. That zero was vacuous. The matcher read only one of the citation shapes the assessments actually use — the CS-2 addendum had warned in writing that there were three — so it was comparing under a quarter of the corpus. With all four shapes supported it compares 300 pairs and finds these 43 (Iteration 79). REMEDIATION IS FOUNDER'S (CS-2b): these are published briefings and §1c forbids editing them, so each needs a dated correction rather than a silent retier. The list is shrink-only, so an entry can only leave once that correction exists.",
